"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M20 12h2"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m6.34 17.66-1.41 1.41"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m19.07 4.93-1.41 1.41"},"children":[]}]},{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"17","height":"17","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-moon life-theme-icon-dark","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M12 3a6 6 0 0 0 9 9 9 9 0 1 1-9-9Z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-language-switch","aria-label":"English Choose language","aria-haspopup":"menu","aria-expanded":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-globe","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M12 2a14.5 14.5 0 0 0 0 20 14.5 14.5 0 0 0 0-20"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M2 12h20"},"children":[]}]},{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["English"]},{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-down","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m6 9 6 6 6-6"},"children":[]}]}]}]},{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-account","href":"/en/sign-in"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"17","height":"17","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-circle-user-round","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M18 20a6 6 0 0 0-12 0"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"10","r":"4"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"},"children":[]}]},{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Sign in to sync"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"main","props":{"className":"life-reader life-tip-layout"},"children":[{"tag":"aside","props":{"className":"life-reader-sidebar life-tip-sidebar"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-back-link","href":"/en/book/31"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-left","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m12 19-7-7 7-7"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M19 12H5"},"children":[]}]},"Back to index"]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-sidebar-caption"},"children":["What options are available after turning 18?"]},{"tag":"nav","props":{"aria-label":"Chapter entries"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/31-01"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["01"]},"First, check the eligibility criteria: the age and education requirements for all twelve pathways are clearly stated in official documents"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/31-02"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["02"]},"Men who turn 18 must complete military service registration by October 31; mandatory active duty lasts two years"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/31-03"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["03"]},"Refusing military service after enlistment: no travel abroad, no further education, and barred from civil service and state-owned enterprises for two years"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/31-04"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["04"]},"Two main benefits for college students joining the military: up to 20,000 RMB per year for tuition, two-year extension of student status, and a special postgraduate admission program"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/31-05"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["05"]},"Only six scenarios allow the government to assign jobs after discharge; those opting for self-employment must register within 30 days"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"aria-current":"page","className":"active","href":"/en/tip/31-06","data-status":"active"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["06"]},"Three key financial aspects after discharge: one-time separation pay, military service counting toward work seniority, and tax deductions for self-employed veterans"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/31-07"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["07"]},"There’s more than just civil service exams to get into the government system: serving two years in grassroots programs qualifies you for a special recruitment quota of 10% each year"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/31-08"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["08"]},"Teachers in the Special Post Program who complete three years of service, pass evaluations, and wish to stay should be promptly added to the official teaching staff"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/31-09"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["09"]},"Firefighters and civilian personnel in the military represent two additional pathways for public recruitment, with lower entry requirements than civil service exams"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/31-10"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["10"]},"Education is not a one-time deal: self-study exams have no age or prior education limits; both adult college entrance exams and open universities offer pathways to further education"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/31-11"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["11"]},"Not joining a company means you must arrange your own social insurance: you’ll need to enroll in pension and medical plans at your place of work, as household registration restrictions have now been lifted"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/31-12"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["12"]},"Food delivery workers, ride‑hailing drivers, and local freight carriers all get occupational injury coverage paid for by the platform on a per‑order basis — at no cost to them"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/31-13"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["13"]},"Two pathways to secure a government job on the day you fill out college applications: government-funded teacher training and targeted medical student programs, at the cost of a six-year service commitment"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/31-14"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["14"]},"Before going abroad to work, check whether the company has a license for international labor cooperation: it is illegal for them to demand a deposit from you"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/31-15"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["15"]},"Working remotely for a foreign company from home: this income is considered domestic earnings for tax purposes; you must file your own individual income tax returns, and incoming payments should be reported as “employee compensation”"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/31-16"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["16"]},"Starting a business without joining a company? First look at startup guarantee loans: up to 300,000 RMB per individual, with the government covering half the interest"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-tip-page"},"children":[{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-breadcrumb","aria-label":"Breadcrumb"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book"},"children":["Explore the book"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"aria-hidden":"true"},"children":["/"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book/31"},"children":["Chapter 31"," ·"," ","What options are available after turning 18?"]}]},{"tag":"article","props":{"className":"life-entry-card status-unmarked is-standalone","id":"31-06"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-top"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-entry-number"},"children":["06"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-evidence grade-a"},"children":["Evidence"," ","A"]}]},{"tag":"h1","props":{"lang":"en"},"children":["Three key financial aspects after discharge: one-time separation pay, military service counting toward work seniority, and tax deductions for self-employed veterans"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"lang":"en","className":"life-entry-summary"},"children":["After leaving the military, three main financial factors matter. First, there is a one-time separation payment for veterans who choose to work independently; the amount depends on how many years you served, with additional bonuses for those who earned commendations. Second, your military service years count toward your overall work seniority, allowing them to be combined with any pre- or post-discharge work history for social insurance purposes. Third, if you start your own business, you may qualify for tax deductions of up to 20,000 yuan per year for three years."]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-impact"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["There are no direct costs involved. Upon discharge, the mi…"]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["The first benefit is outlined in the Regulations on the Resettlement of Veterans: “Veterans who choose to work…"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-actions","aria-label":"Mark: Three key financial aspects after discharge: one-time separation pay, military service counting toward work seniority, and tax deductions for self-employed veterans"},"children":[{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action done","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-check","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M20 6 9 17l-5-5"},"children":[]}]},"Done"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action todo","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-list-todo","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"rect","props":{"x":"3","y":"5","width":"6","height":"6","rx":"1"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m3 17 2 2 4-4"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 6h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 12h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 18h8"},"children":[]}]},"Plan to do"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action favorite","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-bookmark","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m19 21-7-4-7 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h10a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v16z"},"children":[]}]},"Save"]}," ",{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"social-share-trigger"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-share2 lucide-share-2","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"5","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"6","cy":"12","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"19","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"8.59","x2":"15.42","y1":"13.51","y2":"17.49"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"15.41","x2":"8.59","y1":"6.51","y2":"10.49"},"children":[]}]},"Share this tip"]}]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-detail-toggle","aria-expanded":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"10","height":"10","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"currentColor","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-circle","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"},"children":[]}]},"Hide details"]},{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-down rotated","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m6 9 6 6 6-6"},"children":[]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-details"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["There are no direct costs involved. Upon discharge, the military transfers your social insurance records and payments to you, and you then register these with the local social insurance office."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["The first benefit is outlined in the Regulations on the Resettlement of Veterans: “Veterans who choose to work independently receive a one-time separation payment based on their years of service.” This payment is funded by the central government, with specific amounts determined by relevant authorities and adjusted periodically. Additional bonuses are provided in five tiers: 25% for recipients of medals or honorary titles, 20% for those with first-class combat achievements or first-level commendations, 15% for second-class combat achievements or first-level commendations, 10% for third-class combat achievements or second-level commendations, and 5% for fourth-class combat achievements or third-level commendations. The regulations also state that veterans who do not find employment immediately may claim unemployment benefits, with their military service years counted toward insurance contributions, except for those placed in retirement or supported through other programs. The second benefit comes from the Veterans Protection Law: “Military service years are counted toward overall work seniority, which is then combined with any subsequent work history.” This seniority is also factored into pension, medical, and unemployment insurance calculations, and veterans’ service is recognized as equivalent to grassroots work experience under the Military Insurance Law. Finally, a 2023 joint announcement by the Ministry of Finance, State Taxation Administration, and Veterans Affairs Ministry allows self-employed veterans to deduct up to 20,000 yuan per year from their taxes for three years, with a possible 20% increase; this amount is subtracted from the total tax owed rather than provided as a cash payment. Employers hiring veterans may also receive a deduction of up to 6,000 yuan per employee per year, with a 50% increase possible. These provisions are effective from January 1, 2023, through December 31, 2027. It is important to note that this tax benefit is separate from any local “one-time economic subsidies” provided by individual regions, which are determined independently and may vary widely."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Original sources"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":["国务院、中央军委 (2024). 退役军人安置条例（国务院、中央军委令第 787 号，第二十一、二十二、七十四、八十一、八十五条）. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.gov.cn/gongbao/2024/issue_11526/202408/content_6969192.html","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://www.gov.cn/gongbao/2024/issue_11526/202408/content_6969192.html"]},"；退役军人事务部 (2020). 关于一次性退役金的十个问题（转载《中国退役军人》2020 年第 10 期）：「基本标准。士兵服现役每满一年，发给4500元」「退役金标准适时调整」. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.mva.gov.cn/sy/zzxc/202011/t20201113_43153.html","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://www.mva.gov.cn/sy/zzxc/202011/t20201113_43153.html"]},"；贵州省退役军人事务厅 (2024). 一次性退役金增发，重要变化！：「现在执行的标准是：士兵服现役每满一年，发给4500元」. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"http://tyjrswt.guizhou.gov.cn/zfxxgk/fdzdgknr/zdlyxx_5621158/tyaz_5621161/202408/t20240809_85367194.html","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["http://tyjrswt.guizhou.gov.cn/zfxxgk/fdzdgknr/zdlyxx_5621158/tyaz_5621161/202408/t20240809_85367194.html"]},"；烟台市牟平区人民政府 (2025). 答复中引《烟台市退役军人事务局、烟台市财政局关于调整自主就业退役士兵一次性经济补助标准的通知》：「2024年退出现役的每服役一年补助6000元」. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.muping.gov.cn/art/2025/11/10/art_105032_2960250.html","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://www.muping.gov.cn/art/2025/11/10/art_105032_2960250.html"]},"；全国人大常委会 (2020). 退役军人保障法（第四十二、四十四、五十条）. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/fgwx/flfg/16048597.html","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["http://www.mod.gov.cn/gfbw/fgwx/flfg/16048597.html"]},"（国防部刊登）；全国人大常委会 (2012). 军人保险法（第十六、二十三条）. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://flk.npc.gov.cn/detail?id=2c909fdd678bf17901678bf73e160645","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://flk.npc.gov.cn/detail?id=2c909fdd678bf17901678bf73e160645"]},"（国家法律法规数据库）；财政部、税务总局、退役军人事务部 (2023). 关于进一步扶持自主就业退役士兵创业就业有关税收政策的公告（2023 年第 14 号）. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.gov.cn/zhengce/zhengceku/202308/content_6896456.htm","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://www.gov.cn/zhengce/zhengceku/202308/content_6896456.htm"]}]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.gov.cn/gongbao/2024/issue_11526/202408/content_6969192.html","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"life-source-link"},"children":["Open source link"," ",{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"13","height":"13","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M15 3h6v6"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M10 14 21 3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"},"children":[]}]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Book note"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-content-reference"},"children":["The regulations only state that the specific amount shall be separately determined by the competent authorities. The only official figure available can be found in the Ministry of Veterans Affairs' official website 2020 annual publication, which states: \"For every full year of active service, 4500 yuan shall be paid,\" and also notes that it will be \"adjusted accordingly.\" The increased proportion mentioned in that article no longer aligns with the current regulations; the regulations shall prevail. A publication from the Guizhou Provincial Department of Veterans Affairs in 2024 year 8 month still states under the new regulations: \"The standard currently in effect is: For every full year of active service, soldiers shall be paid 4500 yuan.\" TODO (To be verified: No formal standard document has been found; can only confirm that provincial departments were still writing this as of 2024 year 8 month). Additionally, do not confuse this with the local \"one-time economic subsidy.\" That is another sum of money determined and distributed by local authorities themselves; for example, in Yantai, for those retired in 2024 year, there is a subsidy of 6000 yuan for every year of service. Most of the new figures found in guides lack a source, as some simply conflate these two different payments. During the period of conscript service, families are also eligible to receive an additional family preferential allowance. The Military Service Law only states that 'the standards shall be formulated by the local people's government, and the central finance shall provide a fixed quota of subsidies'; for the specific amount, you must ask the county-level people's government that approved your enlistment. Regarding the tax portion, it refers to the maximum amount of tax that can be reduced each year. If a business does not scale up, the full amount cannot be utilized, so the overall scale of benefits is only rated as 'Medium'. The 'Regulations on Promoting the Employment and Entrepreneurship of Veterans' implemented from 2026 year 8 month 1 day adds another provision: professional qualification certificates for skilled personnel obtained during the period of service are universally recognized nationwide after discharge."]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-personal-note"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["My note"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button"},"children":["Write a reminder for yourself…"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager-link","href":"/en/tip/31-05"},"children":[{"tag":"svg